// quantum — Quantum computing with linear types and epistemic uncertainty
//
// The no-cloning theorem enforced at compile time via linear types:
// a Qubit must be consumed exactly once. Includes VQE simulation
// with GUM-compliant uncertainty propagation through gate angles.
// Classical statevector simulation; not a quantum computer.
//
// Submodules:
//   linear        — Linear Qubit type, gates (H, X, Y, Z, S, T, CNOT, CZ, SWAP),
//                   measurement, Bell, GHZ3, teleport; simulator cap 10 qubits
//   vqe           — Variational Quantum Eigensolver with Pauli Hamiltonians and ansatz circuits
//   epistemic_vqe — VQE with gate-angle uncertainty propagation (statevector simulation)

// linear — types: Qubit (linear), QuantumState, QubitPair, QubitTriple,
//   MeasurementResult, TeleportResult, StateInfo
// Constants: QUANTUM_MAX_QUBITS = 10, QUANTUM_MAX_AMPLITUDES = 1024
//   (11th qubit_alloc panics)
// Key fns: quantum_state_new, qubit_alloc,
//   hadamard, pauli_x, pauli_y, pauli_z, s_gate, t_gate, cnot, cz, swap,
//   qubit_measure (not `measure`: that name is a compiler builtin),
//   bell_pair, ghz3, teleport, quantum_state_info,
//   amp_real, amp_imag, amp_prob
// Rx/Ry/Rz are on Statevector in epistemic_vqe, not on linear Qubit.

// vqe — types: PauliOp, PauliString, Hamiltonian, Circuit, HardwareEfficient, UCCSD, VQEResult
// Key fns: h2_hamiltonian, lih_hamiltonian, beh2_hamiltonian

// epistemic_vqe — types: Statevector, EpistemicStatevector, VQEResult
// Key fns: sv_zero, sv_apply_rx, sv_apply_ry, sv_apply_rz, sv_apply_h, sv_apply_cx,
//   vqe_optimize, vqe_epistemic, h2_hamiltonian
